## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/checkerboard.html
- Summary (EN): Generates a pattern of alternating even and odd coloured squares formed by crossing horizontal and vertical divisions, for example a checkered floor tile. Its size_ref input only sets output size and metadata.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud checkerboard génère un damier de carrés pairs et impairs, dont les lignes, les colonnes et la taille de tuile sont réglables.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata; does not control square placement"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "Sets the output layer type"}, {"name": "Rows / Columns", "meaning": "Number of vertical and horizontal divisions; both default to 8"}, {"name": "Even Color", "meaning": "Colour of the even squares; default 1, 1, 1, 1"}, {"name": "Odd Color", "meaning": "Colour of the odd squares; default 0, 0, 0, 0"}, {"name": "Offset", "meaning": "Position of the pattern centre in image space; default 0, 0"}, {"name": "Bias", "meaning": "Shift of the pattern as a fraction of one square's size; default 0, 0"}, {"name": "Tile Size", "meaning": "Size of each square in image space, repeated as a tile; default 2, 2"}]

- Caveats: ["size_ref does not affect square placement; use Offset and Bias for that", "The page does not explain how Rows / Columns interact with Tile Size, so the combined square size is not specified"]

